<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="QueryFlag: Troubleshooting" id="QueryFlag-Troubleshooting">

    <primary-label ref="queryflag"/>
    <show-structure for="chapter" depth="2"/>

    <tldr>
        <p>Settings: <ui-path>Settings | Tools | Database | QueryFlag</ui-path> (DataGrip: <ui-path>Settings | Database | QueryFlag</ui-path>)</p>
        <p>Report a bug: <control>Report Exception</control> in the IDE error dialog</p>
    </tldr>

    <link-summary>Fix common QueryFlag problems: a missing menu, missing results, a data source that is not found, validation errors, and failing queries.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Fix a missing menu, missing results, data source errors, validation messages, and failing queries.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>Troubleshoot the QueryFlag plugin in JetBrains IDEs: missing Query Flag in DB menu, missing query results, DataSource not found, validation errors, and SQL errors.</web-summary>

    <p>
        Find the symptom below and follow the steps to fix it.
    </p>

    <chapter title="Query Flag in DB is missing from the context menu" id="menu-missing">
        <p>The editor context menu shows <control>Query Flag in DB</control> only when at least one template can run in the current project.</p>
        <list>
            <li>
                If you have no templates yet, <a href="QueryFlag-Create-Templates.topic">create one</a>.
            </li>
            <li>
                If your templates use a data source of another project, open that project and make the data source global
                (see <a href="QueryFlag-Create-Templates.topic" anchor="template-scope"/>),
                or create a template for a data source of this project.
            </li>
            <li>
                Make sure the Database Tools and SQL plugin and QueryFlag are enabled in <ui-path>Settings | Plugins</ui-path>.
                The IDE disables QueryFlag when it has no active trial or license; see <a href="QueryFlag-Installation.topic" anchor="license"/>.
            </li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="The query results do not appear" id="no-results">
        <p>
            By default, QueryFlag runs the query in a new query console that does not open in the editor.
            Look for the results in the <control>Services</control> tool window.
        </p>
        <list>
            <li>
                Select <ui-path>View | Tool Windows | Services</ui-path> (<shortcut>Alt+8</shortcut>, macOS: <shortcut>⌘ 8</shortcut>)
                and look under the template's data source.
            </li>
            <li>
                If the <control>Services</control> tool window does not open after a run, make sure that
                <control>Show Services tool window for query execution output</control> is not set to <control>Never</control> in
                <ui-path>Settings | Tools | Database | Query Execution | Output and Results</ui-path>
                (DataGrip: <ui-path>Settings | Database | Query Execution | Output and Results</ui-path>).
            </li>
            <li>
                If QueryFlag shows the warning "Query with blank text is disable, skipping execution", see <a anchor="blank-text-warning"/>.
            </li>
            <li>
                If the data source cannot connect, you get a connection error instead of results.
                See <a anchor="connection"/>.
            </li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="A template shows DataSource not found" id="datasource-not-found">
        <p>
            The settings list shows the red text "DataSource not found, please check your Databases settings"
            for a template whose data source is not available in the current project.
            This happens when the template belongs to another project, or when the data source was deleted and created again.
            Templates refer to data sources by ID, so renaming a data source does not cause it.
        </p>
        <!-- planned-image src="queryflag_datasource_not_found.png" alt="QueryFlag template whose data source is missing, shown in red" -->
        <p>
            If the template belongs to another project, leave it as it is; it works there.
            To use it in this project too, make its data source global; see <a href="QueryFlag-Create-Templates.topic" anchor="template-scope"/>.
            Otherwise, connect it to a data source of this project:
        </p>
        <procedure title="Connect the template to a data source" id="fix-datasource">
            <step>
                In <ui-path>Settings | Tools | Database | QueryFlag</ui-path>, select the template and click <control>Edit</control>.
            </step>
            <step>
                Select a data source in <control>DataSource</control> and click <control>OK</control>.
            </step>
            <step>
                Click <control>Apply</control>.
            </step>
        </procedure>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="The template dialog does not accept the query" id="validation-errors">
        <p>When you click <control>OK</control> in the <control>Add a QueryFlag Entry</control> dialog, QueryFlag checks the fields:</p>
        <deflist type="wide">
            <def title="QueryFlagName cannot be empty" id="error-name">
                Enter a <control>Name</control>.
            </def>
            <def title="Database cannot be empty" id="error-datasource">
                Select a <control>DataSource</control>.
                If the list is empty, add a data source in the <control>Database</control> tool window first.
            </def>
            <def title="Database query cannot be empty" id="error-query">
                Enter a query in <control>QueryFlag with Token</control>.
            </def>
            <def title="Database query must contain at least one &lt;QFToken&gt; replacement" id="error-token">
                Add the token <code>&lt;QUERY_FLAG_TOKEN&gt;</code> to the query.
                The message says <code>&lt;QFToken&gt;</code>, but the token that QueryFlag replaces is <code>&lt;QUERY_FLAG_TOKEN&gt;</code>.
            </def>
        </deflist>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="QueryFlag skips the run because the selection is blank" id="blank-text-warning">
        <p>
            QueryFlag shows the warning "Query with blank text is disable, skipping execution".
            You ran a template with an empty selection, or a selection with only spaces.
            Select the value in the editor and run the template again.
        </p>
        <p>
            QueryFlag also treats the selection as empty in editors that do not show a file, such as the diff viewer.
            Run the template from an editor tab instead.
        </p>
        <p>
            To run templates with an empty value on purpose, select <control>Allow blank Text</control> in the
            <a href="QueryFlag-Settings.topic">QueryFlag settings</a>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="The query fails with an error" id="syntax-error">
        <list>
            <li>
                Make sure the template quotes the token where the query needs a string literal, for example
                <code>WHERE key = '&lt;QUERY_FLAG_TOKEN&gt;'</code>.
                See <a href="QueryFlag-Create-Templates.topic" anchor="token-rules"/>.
            </li>
            <li>
                If the selected value contains a single quote, the SQL string ends early.
                Select only the part of the value without the quote.
            </li>
            <li>
                If the database reports that a table does not exist, or that no schema or database is selected,
                qualify the table name in the template with its schema or database, for example <code>demo.customers</code>.
                Each run uses a new query console, and its current schema can differ from the one in the console where you wrote the query.
            </li>
            <li>
                To see the exact query that ran, select <control>Open console editor</control> in the
                <a href="QueryFlag-Settings.topic">QueryFlag settings</a> and run the template again.
            </li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Add Query Flag is missing from the context menu" id="add-query-flag-missing">
        <p>
            <control>Add Query Flag</control> appears only in an editor that is connected to a data source, such as a query console,
            and only when you select some text first.
            To create a template from a query in another file, copy the query into a query console of the data source,
            or <a href="QueryFlag-Create-Templates.topic" anchor="add-template">add the template in Settings</a>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="The query field highlights the wrong language" id="wrong-highlighting">
        <p>
            The query field uses the query language of the data source that is selected when the dialog opens.
            Save the template, then open it again with <control>Edit</control>: the field now uses the language of the template's data source.
            You can also <a href="QueryFlag-Create-Templates.topic" anchor="create-from-console">create the template from a query console</a> of that data source.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="The query does not connect" id="connection">
        <p>
            QueryFlag runs the query through the data source of the <control>Database</control> tool window.
            If the data source cannot connect, for example because its driver files are missing or its credentials are wrong,
            check the data source:
        </p>
        <procedure title="Test the data source connection" id="test-connection">
            <step>
                In the <control>Database</control> tool window, right-click the data source and select <control>Properties</control>.
            </step>
            <step>
                Click <control>Test Connection</control>.
            </step>
            <step>
                Fix the reported problem and click <control>OK</control>.
            </step>
        </procedure>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Report a problem" id="report">
        <p>
            If the IDE shows a QueryFlag error, click <control>Report Exception</control> in the error dialog.
            For details and other ways to get help, see <a href="QueryFlag-Reference-and-Support.topic" anchor="feature_request_and_bug"/>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

